# GenBioCa — Cursor rules

The authoritative constraints live in `/CLAUDE.md` at the repo root. Read it before
non-trivial work and follow it exactly. Key rules, repeated here so they always apply:

## Active runtime — the ONLY code to develop
- `frontend/` (React 19 + Vite + TS, react-router-dom library/data mode)
- `backend/` (Express 5 + TS + Prisma, schema at `backend/prisma/schema.prisma`)
- `docker-compose.yml`

## Dormant — do NOT edit, import, wire in, or delete
`legacy/src/`, `legacy/prisma/`, `legacy/tests/` (old Node backend),
`legacy/legacy_python_backend/`, and stray prototype HTML copies at the repo root
(referenced by Vite/Express/Docker — leave them in place). Preserved for
reference only. Never import from these into `frontend/` or `backend/`.

## Non-negotiables
- Backend is the source of truth for authorization and tenant isolation. Frontend
  checks are UX only.
- Every tenant-owned query filters by the authenticated tenant from JWT context.
  Never trust a tenant id from the request body or query alone. Cross-tenant access
  must fail, and gets a negative test.
- Shared masters are global (no `tenant_id`): `frameworks`, `framework_rules`,
  `kpi_definitions`, `permissions`.
- `audit_events` are append-only (DB trigger `prevent_audit_event_mutation`). Never
  add update/delete APIs for them.
- KPI target met → no risk record. Target missed → exactly ONE linked Major/Minor risk
  for that actual. KPI risk class (Major/Minor) and enterprise risk level
  (Low/Medium/High/Critical) stay SEPARATE fields.
- Approved-evidence gates (KPI approval, policy approval, gap closure, CAPA closure,
  risk-treatment completion) are enforced in the backend, never the UI.
- Traceability order: Policy → Framework → Rule → Evidence → Control → KPI →
  Target vs Actual → Risk.
- Prototype-only routes must show: “Prototype module — demonstration data only.
  Changes are not saved.” Live API-backed routes must not. Never fake a backend write.

## React Router — stay in library/data mode
No `@react-router/dev` / `@react-router/node` / `@react-router/serve`, no
`reactRouter()` Vite plugin, no `react-router.config.*`, no `app/routes.ts`
file-system routing, no `ssr: true`, no RSC or server actions. CI enforces this.

## Security
- Access token in memory; refresh token in HTTP-only cookie, hashed in DB, rotating,
  with family reuse detection. Do not weaken.
- Never commit or print secrets. `.env`, `.env.local`, `backend/.env` stay gitignored.
- Integration tests use `DATABASE_URL_TEST` only; they must refuse the dev DB.
- No auto-seeding on startup. Zod-validate API boundaries; never leak Prisma errors.

## Workflow
Branch → small focused commits → local checks (typecheck, lint, tests,
`prisma validate`, frontend build + Playwright) → private branch → DRAFT PR →
CodeRabbit → human review → merge. Never auto-merge. Never
`npm audit fix --force`. No broad unrelated dependency upgrades.

## Style
No broad cosmetic “make it look less AI-generated” refactors. Priority order:
correctness → security → tenant isolation → tests → maintainability → cleanup.
Anonymized data only (Company 001, User 003, KPI-001, RSK-042; `.test` emails).
